{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1558284-text-based-wod-game","id":1558284,"title":"Text Based WoD Game!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-13T07:03:12-08:00","id":1558284,"title":"Text Based WoD Game!","content":"So, due to troubles with my gaming PC's graphics card, I found myself getting back onto the MUD (Multi User Dungeon) kick for the first time in decades, and I stumbled across this particular game.<br /> <br /> <b>Haven of the Embraced:</b> <a href=\"https://www.mudverse.com/game/571\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.mudverse.com/game/571</a><br /> <br /> It's an MUD that's set in the <i>Dark Ages WoD</i>, roughly a couple centuries prior to the formation of sects like Camarilla, Anarchs or Sabbat. I understand that it's relatively new, and still undergoing development, but enough of it has been completed so far that the game is mostly playable.<br /> <br /> Players have the option to start their character as either a Human, or a Vampire of almost any clan. Tzimisce, Cappadocian and Lasombra are restricted, and need to have their embrace role played out before you can join them.<br /> <br /> Character progression is done through the Remort system, where each time you reach level 100, you can remort back down to level 1 and gain 3 Freebie points to spend on your character sheet. Those who choose to start out as Humans can also become Werewolves or Mages; which foregoes the 3 Freebie points, but allows you to essentially remake your character as a different splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Diablerie is not in the game, but you can reduce your Generation through freebie points. With an upwards cap of 5th generation for the most dedicated players. However, going below 9th generation requires 30 Freebies and a minimum amount of previous remorts. Also, no matter what generation your sire is, all embraced vampires begin the game as 10th generation. So if you were thinking of trying to speed run the process by finding a low generation sire, you're out of luck.<br /> <br /> Lastly, vampire players get 24 hours of active play time immunity to sunlight, before it start doing actual damage. This should give newcomers plenty of time to familiarize themselves with the game's lay out and mechanics, before they have to worry about seeking shelter from the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}